@prefix : <http://example.org/act-gravity/> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix pe: <https://eyereasoner.github.io/pe#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

:run :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath .
:run :pathMediator :gravityMediator .
:run :supports :InformationTransferInterface .
:run :supports :LocalReadoutInterface .
:gravityMediator a :NonClassicalMediator .
:run :can :SupportMediatorOnlyEntanglementWitness .
:run :supportsConclusion :MediatorNonClassical .
:run :rulesOut :PurelyClassicalMediatorModel .
:run :supportsConclusion :GravityMediatorNonClassical .
:case :checkC1 :Passed .
:case :checkC2 :Passed .
:case :checkC3 :Passed .
:case :checkC5 :Passed .
:contrastRun :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath .
:contrastRun :pathMediator :classicalGravityMediator .
:contrastRun :supports :InformationTransferInterface .
:contrastRun :supports :LocalReadoutInterface .
:contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorOnlyEntanglementWitness .
:classicalGravityMediator :cannot :MediateEntanglementUnderWitnessConditions .
:case :checkC4 :Passed .
:case :checkC6 :Passed .
:case :checkC7 :Passed .
:case :checkC8 :Passed .
:case :checkC9 :Passed .
:case :checkC10 :Passed .
:case :checkC11 :Passed .
:case :checkC12 :Passed .
:contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorNonClassicalConclusion .
:case :checkC13 :Passed .
:case :checkC14 :Passed .
:out log:outputString "ACT gravity mediator witness\n\n## Answer\nYES for the mediator-only witness run.\nNO for a purely classical mediator model under the same mediator-only conditions.\n\n## Reason Why\nThe positive run assumes locality and interoperability, excludes direct coupling between the two quantum systems, and records an entanglement witness after interaction through the mediator alone. Under those constructor-theoretic conditions, the mediator must be non-classical, so the run rules out a purely classical mediator model. The contrast run keeps the same locality, interoperability, and mediator-only structure but assigns the mediator a purely classical model. In that case the mediator-only entanglement witness is blocked, so the run cannot support the same non-classicality conclusion.\n\n## Check\nC1  OK - locality is assumed in the positive run\nC2  OK - interoperability is assumed in the positive run\nC3  OK - direct coupling between the two quantum systems is excluded\nC4  OK - the positive run has a mediator-only interaction path\nC5  OK - an entanglement witness is observed in the positive run\nC6  OK - the positive run supports an information-transfer interface\nC7  OK - the positive run supports local readout\nC8  OK - the positive mediator is derived to be non-classical\nC9  OK - a purely classical mediator model is ruled out by the positive run\nC10 OK - the non-classicality conclusion applies to the gravitational mediator\nC11 OK - the contrast run is also mediator-only\nC12 OK - the contrast run cannot support a mediator-only entanglement witness\nC13 OK - the purely classical gravitational mediator cannot mediate entanglement under the witness conditions\nC14 OK - the contrast run cannot support the non-classicality conclusion\n" .

{ :run :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . }
  pe:rule 1;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :assumes :Locality . },
    { :run :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . },
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . }.

{ :run a :ExperimentRun . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :assumes :Locality . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :pathMediator :gravityMediator . }
  pe:rule 1;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :assumes :Locality . },
    { :run :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . },
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . }.

{ :run :supports :InformationTransferInterface . }
  pe:rule 2;
  pe:binding [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :run :controlStatus :CopyLikeControlPresent . }.

{ :run :assumes :Interoperability . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :controlStatus :CopyLikeControlPresent . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :supports :LocalReadoutInterface . }
  pe:rule 3;
  pe:binding [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :probeStatus :LocalProbeReadoutPresent . }.

{ :run :probeStatus :LocalProbeReadoutPresent . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :gravityMediator a :NonClassicalMediator . }
  pe:rule 4;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :assumes :Locality . },
    { :run :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :run :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . },
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . },
    { :run :observed :EntanglementWitnessPassed . }.

{ :run :observed :EntanglementWitnessPassed . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :run :can :SupportMediatorOnlyEntanglementWitness . }
  pe:rule 4;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :assumes :Locality . },
    { :run :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :run :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . },
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . },
    { :run :observed :EntanglementWitnessPassed . }.

{ :run :supportsConclusion :MediatorNonClassical . }
  pe:rule 4;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :run :assumes :Locality . },
    { :run :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :run :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . },
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . },
    { :run :observed :EntanglementWitnessPassed . }.

{ :run :rulesOut :PurelyClassicalMediatorModel . }
  pe:rule 5;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run :supportsConclusion :MediatorNonClassical . },
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . },
    { :gravityMediator a :NonClassicalMediator . }.

{ :run :supportsConclusion :GravityMediatorNonClassical . }
  pe:rule 6;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :gravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :run ];
  pe:uses
    { :run :usesMediator :gravityMediator . },
    { :gravityMediator :couplingMode :Gravitational . },
    { :gravityMediator a :NonClassicalMediator . }.

{ :gravityMediator :couplingMode :Gravitational . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :case :checkC1 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 9;
  pe:uses { :run :assumes :Locality . }.

{ :case :checkC2 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 10;
  pe:uses { :run :assumes :Interoperability . }.

{ :case :checkC3 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 11;
  pe:uses { :run :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . }.

{ :case :checkC5 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 13;
  pe:uses { :run :observed :EntanglementWitnessPassed . }.

{ :contrastRun :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . }
  pe:rule 1;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :classicalGravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses
    { :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Locality . },
    { :contrastRun :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . },
    { :contrastRun :usesMediator :classicalGravityMediator . }.

{ :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :assumes :Locality . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :usesMediator :classicalGravityMediator . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :pathMediator :classicalGravityMediator . }
  pe:rule 1;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :classicalGravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses
    { :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Locality . },
    { :contrastRun :directCouplingStatus :NoDirectCoupling . },
    { :contrastRun :usesMediator :classicalGravityMediator . }.

{ :contrastRun :supports :InformationTransferInterface . }
  pe:rule 2;
  pe:binding [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses
    { :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :contrastRun :controlStatus :CopyLikeControlPresent . }.

{ :contrastRun :assumes :Interoperability . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :controlStatus :CopyLikeControlPresent . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :supports :LocalReadoutInterface . }
  pe:rule 3;
  pe:binding [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses
    { :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :contrastRun :probeStatus :LocalProbeReadoutPresent . }.

{ :contrastRun :probeStatus :LocalProbeReadoutPresent . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorOnlyEntanglementWitness . }
  pe:rule 7;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :classicalGravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses
    { :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Locality . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :contrastRun :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . },
    { :contrastRun :usesMediator :classicalGravityMediator . },
    { :classicalGravityMediator :mediatorModel :PurelyClassical . }.

{ :classicalGravityMediator :mediatorModel :PurelyClassical . }
  pe:fact "act-gravity-mediator-witness.n3".

{ :classicalGravityMediator :cannot :MediateEntanglementUnderWitnessConditions . }
  pe:rule 7;
  pe:binding
    [ pe:var "M"; pe:value :classicalGravityMediator ],
    [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses
    { :contrastRun a :ExperimentRun . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Locality . },
    { :contrastRun :assumes :Interoperability . },
    { :contrastRun :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . },
    { :contrastRun :usesMediator :classicalGravityMediator . },
    { :classicalGravityMediator :mediatorModel :PurelyClassical . }.

{ :case :checkC4 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 12;
  pe:uses { :run :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . }.

{ :case :checkC6 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 14;
  pe:uses { :run :supports :InformationTransferInterface . }.

{ :case :checkC7 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 15;
  pe:uses { :run :supports :LocalReadoutInterface . }.

{ :case :checkC8 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 16;
  pe:uses { :gravityMediator a :NonClassicalMediator . }.

{ :case :checkC9 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 17;
  pe:uses { :run :rulesOut :PurelyClassicalMediatorModel . }.

{ :case :checkC10 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 18;
  pe:uses { :run :supportsConclusion :GravityMediatorNonClassical . }.

{ :case :checkC11 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 19;
  pe:uses { :contrastRun :interactionPath :MediatorOnlyPath . }.

{ :case :checkC12 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 20;
  pe:uses { :contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorOnlyEntanglementWitness . }.

{ :contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorNonClassicalConclusion . }
  pe:rule 8;
  pe:binding [ pe:var "R"; pe:value :contrastRun ];
  pe:uses { :contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorOnlyEntanglementWitness . }.

{ :case :checkC13 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 21;
  pe:uses { :classicalGravityMediator :cannot :MediateEntanglementUnderWitnessConditions . }.

{ :case :checkC14 :Passed . }
  pe:rule 22;
  pe:uses { :contrastRun :cannot :SupportMediatorNonClassicalConclusion . }.

{ :out log:outputString "ACT gravity mediator witness\n\n## Answer\nYES for the mediator-only witness run.\nNO for a purely classical mediator model under the same mediator-only conditions.\n\n## Reason Why\nThe positive run assumes locality and interoperability, excludes direct coupling between the two quantum systems, and records an entanglement witness after interaction through the mediator alone. Under those constructor-theoretic conditions, the mediator must be non-classical, so the run rules out a purely classical mediator model. The contrast run keeps the same locality, interoperability, and mediator-only structure but assigns the mediator a purely classical model. In that case the mediator-only entanglement witness is blocked, so the run cannot support the same non-classicality conclusion.\n\n## Check\nC1  OK - locality is assumed in the positive run\nC2  OK - interoperability is assumed in the positive run\nC3  OK - direct coupling between the two quantum systems is excluded\nC4  OK - the positive run has a mediator-only interaction path\nC5  OK - an entanglement witness is observed in the positive run\nC6  OK - the positive run supports an information-transfer interface\nC7  OK - the positive run supports local readout\nC8  OK - the positive mediator is derived to be non-classical\nC9  OK - a purely classical mediator model is ruled out by the positive run\nC10 OK - the non-classicality conclusion applies to the gravitational mediator\nC11 OK - the contrast run is also mediator-only\nC12 OK - the contrast run cannot support a mediator-only entanglement witness\nC13 OK - the purely classical gravitational mediator cannot mediate entanglement under the witness conditions\nC14 OK - the contrast run cannot support the non-classicality conclusion\n" . }
  pe:rule 23;
  pe:uses
    { :case :checkC1 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC2 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC3 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC4 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC5 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC6 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC7 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC8 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC9 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC10 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC11 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC12 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC13 :Passed . },
    { :case :checkC14 :Passed . }.
